+# Security notes
+
+This repository is a deliberately vulnerable smoke target. It is never deployed, so there is no
+disclosure process. The entries below record the issues that were fixed in this history, so that
+the record of what changed and why is in one place.
+
+## 2026-03-14: path traversal in `read_report` (CWE-22)
+
+The `report` path joined the client-supplied name onto the report directory and opened the result,
+so a name containing `../` read files outside that directory. `read_report` now canonicalises the
+joined path with `os.path.realpath()` and refuses any result that does not start with the report
+directory before opening it.
+
+## 2026-02-26: command injection in `archive` (CWE-78)
+
+The `archive` path built a `tar` command line from the client-supplied export name and ran it
+through the shell, so shell metacharacters in the name ran arbitrary commands. `archive` now calls
+`shutil.make_archive`, which runs no shell; there is no command string.
+
+## 2026-02-10: Jinja2 2.10 (CVE-2019-10906)
+
+Jinja2 2.10 let a sandboxed template reach `str.format` and escape the sandbox
+(GHSA-462w-v97r-4m45). The pin was raised to 3.1.6, which has no open advisory.
